{"id": 32, "ts": 1781762880.9112258, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the points raised about stress resilience and decision quality. While I originally favored Candidate\u202fA for his operational reliability, the lack of any documented evidence that he can maintain performance under pressure remains a critical gap for long\u2011distance flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC provides concrete safety\u2011critical evidence: he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d demonstrates \u201cexcellent attention skills,\u201d and \u201cputs concern for others above everything.\u201d These facts collectively cover stress resilience, decision quality, crew cooperation, attention to detail, and responsibility\u2014core criteria for this role. Although C has noted communication difficulties and a limited appetite for further education, these concerns are outweighed by his proven ability to make sound, rapid decisions and to foster a cooperative cockpit environment, which are non\u2011negotiable for safety. Therefore, I shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
